{"id":"s2.1.4","slug":"important-fractions","title":"Important Fractions","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Memorizing the decimal and percentage conversions for common fractions is essential for speed, especially in the early parts of the test. The following table omits obvious fractions like 1/2, 1/4, etc., and focuses on those involving sixths, sevenths, eighths, ninths, elevenths, twelfths, and sixteenths. It's helpful to memorize the base fraction (e.g., 1/7) and then derive the others by multiplication.</p>","summary":"Memorizing the decimal and percentage conversions for common fractions is essential for speed, especially in the early parts of the test.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that involves converting a common fraction (e.g., sevenths, eighths, ninths) to a decimal or percentage, or comparing its value.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Convert $12\\frac{1}{2}\\%$ to a fraction.","answer":"1/8","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","conversions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Convert $\\frac{11}{5}$ to a percentage.","answer":"220%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","conversions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Which is larger: $\\frac{5}{9}$ or .56?","answer":".56","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Which is larger: $\\frac{5}{8}$ or .622?","answer":"5/8","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Convert $\\frac{17}{8}$ to a decimal.","answer":"2.125","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $.777... - .333... + .555...$.","answer":"1","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":7,"text":"Convert $\\frac{3}{5}$ to a percentage.","answer":"60%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","conversions"]},{"id":8,"text":"Convert $\\frac{1}{8}$ to a decimal.","answer":".125","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":9,"text":"Which is smaller: $\\frac{9}{11}$ or .81?","answer":".81","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":10,"text":"Convert $\\frac{1}{16}$ t